/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  PROPERTIES & DATA MODE of membrane24 (runCase <case> props): the DSPM-DE
  pore of NF270 FITTED to published measurements, and written as the
  membrane record the Process mode's spiral-wound stage reads.

  THE DATA.  Fernandez de Labastida & Yaroshchuk, "Nanofiltration of
  Multi-Ion Solutions: Quantitative Control of Concentration Polarization
  and Interpretation by Solution-Diffusion-Electro-Migration Model",
  Membranes 11 (2021) 272, doi:10.3390/membranes11040272 (CC BY 4.0):
  NF270 in a rotating-disk cell at 20 C, four dominant salts at 0.01 mol/L,
  INTRINSIC rejections (the authors corrected them for concentration
  polarisation) at seven permeate fluxes each, 6-56 um/s.  The symbols of
  their Figures 1a-4a, digitised by bin/curate/digitise_fdl2021.py and
  written as four datasets by bin/curate/export_fdl2021_rejections.py
  (constant/experimental/fdl2021_<salt>.dat).  The reading error is in each
  file's header; the authors publish no measurement uncertainty, so the fit
  is UNWEIGHTED (a rejection as a fraction).  Not in the feeds: the 2e-4
  mol/L NaNO3 + NH4Cl traces they added (2 % of the dominant salt).

  THE PARTITION.  Fitted: the two CHLORIDES, NaCl and MgCl2 -- one co-ion,
  a monovalent and a divalent counter-ion.  HELD OUT, never seen by the
  fitter: the two SULFATES, Na2SO4 and MgSO4, whose divalent co-ion the
  fitted pore must exclude by its charge and its size alone.
  CHOSEN AFTER MEASURING THE ALTERNATIVES, and said here because it is what
  a reader must weigh: on these four series the identifiability of (r_p,
  X_d) depends on WHICH salts are fitted, and three partitions were run
  before this one --
    fit NaCl + MgSO4    r_p ran to its upper bound (3 nm, X_d -404 mol/m3):
                        a Donnan-only pore, the two not separable; held-out
                        AAD 16 points (notValidated)
    fit NaCl + Na2SO4   correlation(r_p, X_d) = -1.0000: not identifiable
    fit NaCl + MgCl2    identifiable (this case)
  so the verdict below is that of a partition chosen for identifiability,
  not one fixed blind; and the held-out sulfates sit at R 0.977-0.997, where
  a tight pore of any charge predicts them closely -- it is a weak test of
  X_d.  A blind partition would be a separate study.

  THE MODEL.  DSPM-DE (Bowen & Welfoot 2002), its pore SOLVED across 101
  nodes (the default since C141), the Dechadilok-Deen hindrance, ideal
  activities.  The film is NanoFiltran's "no polarisation" (k_film 10 m/s)
  because the data are intrinsic: R = 1 - c_p/c_wall is what the authors
  report and what `rejection intrinsic;` compares.  FREE: the pore radius
  r_p and the fixed charge X_d (either sign); HELD at the base record
  NF270_dspmde's values: the porosity over thickness A_k/dx 5e6 1/m, the
  pore dielectric constant 35 (Born ON) and A_w (not read at an imposed
  J_v).  Freeing A_k/dx or eps_p as well was measured and is not
  identifiable from these data (|correlation| >= 0.99).  The ion radii and D0 are
  the species records' (hydrated radii, the convention NF270_dspmde's own
  header states), corrected to 20 C by Stokes-Einstein on the declared
  liquid viscosity.

  THE RECORD.  `output { record ...; }` writes constant/assets/
  NF270_FdL2021.dat with the fitted values, their 95 % half-widths, the
  verdict and the fingerprints of the four datasets, of this operation's
  block and of the base record.  The Process mode (system/flowsheetDict)
  reads that record and REFUSES it when any fingerprint no longer matches.

  WHAT IS PINNED (expected.props).  The fitted values and their
  uncertainties, the held-out AAD and the verdict: self-recorded rows --
  they pin that the fit has not MOVED, not that NF270 is right.  The
  held-out verdict is the validation claim, and it is the paper's data that
  decide it.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name      fit_NF270_FdL2021;
        type      fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path poreModel.poreRadius;     initial 6.0e-10;  min 3.0e-10;  max 3.0e-9; }
            { path poreModel.chargeDensity;  initial -20;      min -3000;    max 3000;   }
        );

        evidence
        (
            { dataset "constant/experimental/fdl2021_NaCl.dat";   role fit; }
            { dataset "constant/experimental/fdl2021_MgCl2.dat";  role fit; }
            { dataset "constant/experimental/fdl2021_Na2SO4.dat"; role validation; }
            { dataset "constant/experimental/fdl2021_MgSO4.dat";  role validation; }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  10 points;
            origin  "declared before the fit, by this case: a pore model held at ONE fixed charge for four salts is asked to predict the held-out salts within 10 points of rejection on average -- an engineering criterion for a pedagogical characterisation, not a measurement uncertainty (the source publishes none)";
        }

        residual
        {
            kind        membrane;
            model       DSPM-DE;
            membrane    NF270_dspmde;
            rejection   intrinsic;
            weighting   absolute;
            transportParameters
            {
                poreSolver { method finiteDifference; nodes 101; wallClosure porePermeate; }
                hindrance  DechadilokDeen2006;
                activity   ideal;
            }
            k_film      10;      // m/s: no polarisation -- the data are intrinsic
            polarisation { suctionCorrection GeraldesAfonso2006; ionCoupling electroneutral; }
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter     60;
            tolerance   1.0e-10;
            fdStep      1.0e-4;
            lambda0     1.0e-2;
        }

        output
        {
            record   "constant/assets/NF270_FdL2021.dat";
        }
    }
);
